# Normalize line endings in the Git repo to LF.
#
# - `text=auto` lets git decide binary-vs-text per file (binary stays untouched).
# - `eol=lf` stores every text file as LF; git checks out CRLF automatically on
#   Windows, so Windows editors see familiar line endings while the repo stays
#   consistent across macOS / Linux / Windows / CI.
#
# Keep the VS Code `files.eol: "lf"` (see .vscode/settings.json) so saves write LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalize binary assets (would corrupt them). The `* text=auto` above
# already covers them; this is belt-and-braces for files with no obvious ext.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.bin binary
*.pyc binary
